## What to build

After a tutor reply is saved as completed, run one suggestion-model call outside the tutor session with the default suggestion model (the conversation provider's cheap model: Haiku for Claude, Codex Luna for Codex; confirm the Codex model ID). Input: the reply, the preceding learner question and the fixed inherited context. Output: suggestions as exact passages (message, text, canonical offsets), with no proposed question and no cap. Validate and save them with the source message; discard mismatched or overlapping ones. Show a brief nonblocking "Suggestions unavailable" note on failure. Count the call's usage in that reply's token line. Never rerun on reopen or provider switch; no backfill of older replies. Start by reviewing the partial work from the stopped TreeTutor-vm4.11 run, saved as the Git stash `vm4.11-partial` (`git stash show -p stash^{/vm4.11-partial Spec stories 3, 11–13, 17–21, 23–24, 26–27.

Spec: docs/break-down-spec.md (agreed 2026-11-09). Vocabulary: GLOSSARY.md. Size: one fresh context of 100k–150k tokens and under one hour of implementation.`), and reuse what fits; drop the stash once its useful parts are applied.}
